    {
      "id": "setup-and-safe-defaults",
      "name": "Setup and safe defaults",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1100,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Enrich one HubSpot contact, with recoverable writes\n1. Install n8n-nodes-quietpass. Version 0.1.2 is approved; n8n Cloud publication is pending.\n2. Select your QuietPass API credential in its node and HTTP steps. Select a HubSpot Service Key credential with contact read/write access in all CRM HTTP steps. Keep credentials out of Configuration.\n3. Create the 15 qp_phone_* text properties in group quietpass_phone (see guide). Set the two Configuration IDs to your portal and an authorized contact.\n4. Manual-only, paid use OFF, ceiling 0. For a free test select only basic_line_type and enable zero-limit saved workflows in QuietPass. For paid use set explicit ceilings and credit consent in QuietPass, then enable allowPaid and a reviewed ceiling here.\n5. Replace the manual input with a trusted contact-change event for production. One contact per execution; preserve the real phone-history revision. Do not use random IDs or execution time. No historical backfill.\n\nGuide: https://quietpass.com/integrations/n8n/",
        "width": 960,
        "height": 600,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "recovery-instructions",
      "name": "Recovery instructions",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1100,
        700
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## A failed write must not buy another lookup\nThe original operation and quote are saved by QuietPass before execution. On error, keep the failed n8n execution. Copy its operation ID, contact ID, and original phone-history revision into the separate read-only recovery template.\n\nDo not restart a raw stale PATCH or manufacture a new revision. A changed phone or revision prevents the old result from being written. False remains false; unknown clears old QuietPass fields. Pending/expired is not a negative answer.\n\nThe final read and PATCH are separate requests, leaving a small edit window. Stored number, revision receipt, and checked time show what was checked. n8n executions contain contact data: restrict access and set retention.",
        "width": 1000,
        "height": 600,
        "color": 7
      }
    }
  ],
